WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:12.820 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  every day all over the planet millions  of people animals and products come and  go potentially traveling with them a  several known and unknown health threats  such as infectious diseases that can  cross over borders and continents and  endanger public health improving safety  security and protection for all citizens  against health threats our concerns at  the very heart of the European Union's  health policy recent outbreaks such as  the Ebola epidemic or the new emerging  Middle East respiratory syndrome  attesting the European Union's capacity  to respond quickly and efficiently to  these cross-border health threats in  2013 the European Parliament in the 28  member states agreed on a legal  framework on serious cross-border  threats to health call decision 1082  that provides mechanisms and tools to  manage health crises in the EU whilst  individual member states are responsible  for their own health measures decision  1082 supports cooperation and  coordination between member states in  order to fight against cross-border  health threats such as threats of  communicable diseases that can easily  spread from person to person and country  to country  [Music]  and the threat that certain bacteria are  becoming resistant to drugs and  medicines threats of bio toxins from  plants such as ricin that could be used  intentionally to harm people threats of  chemical origin that come from acute  releases of toxic chemical products or  threats caused by environmental events  such as a volcanoes ash clouds or  extreme weather events linked to climate  change decision 1082 encourages all  member states to better prepare for  future outbreaks by sharing their  information sharing their best practices  and ensuring that all their preparedness  plans are compatible consistent and  effective decision 1082 also allows  member states to be part of a new  venture in joint procurement to obtain  medical countermeasures such as vaccines  and medicines furthermore decision 1082  has established epidemiological  surveillance to constantly monitor over  40 communicable diseases across europe  and ad hoc monitoring when health  threats caused by chemical environmental  hazards or biotoxins occur  member states use the early warning and  response system ewr s to immediately  issue alert notifications to the  Commission to member states and to the  World Health Organization w-h-o about  the nature and the location of the  threat concerned in case of an outbreak  it is always vital to know what danger  exactly does the threat posed and what  are the risks for the people in the  European Union European agencies and  scientific committees will carry out  risk assessments of threats to suggest  options and appropriate measures that  can be taken by crisis managers during a  crisis the health security committee HSC  composed of representatives from all of  the 28 member states will consult each  other to coordinate measures to an  outbreak based on the risks involved the  health security committee also consults  on crisis communication to agree upon  messages that can be used by public  health authorities to ensure that both  the general public and healthcare  professionals are provided with clear  consistent coherent information  [Music]  eventually if required international  organizations such as the World Health  Organization will become involved and  international partners from other  countries will be consulted whenever  necessary supported by the Commission  decision 1082 gives us the mechanisms  and tools to manage public health crises  that help us to improve health security  in the European Union solid crisis  preparedness ultimately protects  Europeans against health threats and  prevents additional burdens on European  health systems we cannot anticipate  every disease and every threat but  together we can be prepared for the  worst and be ready to act quickly should  we have to deal with a crisis decision  1082 crisis management for serious  cross-border health threats in the  European Union  [Music]

